m/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T12:30:39Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T13:20:53Z","body":"I managed to fix this by adding a AspectRatioContainer on top of my SubViewportContainer this way all my game always run on the same ratio.\n\nNevertheless, I created a MRP, this not always happens so if you testing please take some time to test it. Move the mouse around a few minutes.\n\nI can't test in 4.3, but I'm pretty sure I had this before aswell, I just tought it would go away eventually with 4.4 updates.\n\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bbda4911-c965-4212-9516-5b351986ee86\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7bd66195-cf96-4efb-b549-6ec23b4b4b73)\n\n[bug_screen_tearing.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18922605/bug_screen_tearing.zip)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676178750/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676984632","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103139#issuecomment-2676984632","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103139","id":2676984632,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fj4s4","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-23T16:51:32Z","updated_at":"2025-02-23T16:51:32Z","body":"> This probably happens because of not setting Snap 2D transform to pixel. The problem is that having this option on makes the game look terrible when walking in high FPS. So I have no idea how to fix this, is there a solution to this problem? How do other games handle this?\n\nSee the documentation: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/rendering/jitter_stutter.html\n\nI suggest enabling physics interpolation too.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676984632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678889858","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103139#issuecomment-2678889858","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103139","id":2678889858,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6frJ2C","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2","html_url":"https://github.com/conde2","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/conde2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T15:51:28Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T15:51:28Z","body":"@Calinou \n\nI did try physics interpolation, but it did not fix the problem with the white line.\n\n### What fixed my issue was:\n1. Having everything in Process, so the viewport and camera are in sync.\n2. Disable  Snap 2D transform in the Viewport, so there is no jittering because movement is in Proccess\n3. Have a AspectRatio in the viewport so the whitelines stops appearing.\n\n\nNot sure if its a bug, buy looks like it is to me. Anyways I will leave to you guys decide if this is a problem or not.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678889858/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2679267086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103139#issuecomment-2679267086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103139","id":2679267086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fsl8O","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T18:06:36Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T18:07:32Z","body":"You have filtering enabled on your textures, so issues are expected when displaying pixel art:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8bd24139-0b1a-43d8-9b6d-391d8009eb3a)\n\nChange `rendering/textures/canvas_textures/default_texture_filter` to **Nearest** in the Project Settings. Also set the stretch mode to `canvas_items` or `viewport` and [stretch scale mode](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/rendering/multiple_resolutions.html#stretch-scale-mode) to `integer` to ensure correct display regardless of the window size.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2679267086/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2694720670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103139#issuecomment-2694720670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103139","id":2694720670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gniye","user":{"login":"conde2","id":2137569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzc1Njk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2137569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","u